30bp in Q1.\n- Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\" in that period, so investors are still buying.\n- I have only that one debt deal. I found nothing on Pellham's leverage or rating headroom.\n\n**Equity markets: weak.**\n- Pellham pulled its C$2.4B share offering on 14 October. Pellham is the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- The same issuance tracker says two utility offerings were cut back in Q3. It names only Pellham's, so I don't know the other utility.\n- Pellham then said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. That suggests a funding constraint.\n- I found nothing on Norvane's equity plans or share prices, so I can't say whether Norvane could issue.\n\n**What this means for the plans:**\n- Norvane can probably fund through bonds at a higher cost.\n- Pellham probably can't fund its plan as filed, because its equity raise failed and debt alone looks insufficient.\n\n**Gaps:** I did not find the actual 2027 capex amounts, which are in the utility tender calendar. So I can't size the funding gap. It is also unclear whether the failed offering was specific to Pellham or market-wide.\n\n**What would change this:** a successful follow-on offering, such as Pellham reopening in Q1 2027.\n\nSources: n7.r1 (debt) and n8.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":2667,"type":"result","duration_ms":49047,"uuid":"1574a1e0-2f6c-4991-b95b-7a6f960d2167","ttft_stream_ms":2217,"time_to_request_ms":468,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":31,"system_prompt":48,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":24,"input_attachments":185,"input_hooks":15,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":29,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":16,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":12,"request_announcements":26,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":7,"message_normalization":12,"client_creation":15,"request_build":18},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_inde